<title>USA: HomeSide unit to issue $200 mln in debt.</title>
<headline>HomeSide unit to issue $200 mln in debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>HomeSide Inc unit Homeside Lending Inc, is expected to issue $200 million in debt via NationsBanc Capital Markets Inc later today, dealers said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The Baa2/BBB rated deal is expected to consist of seven-year senior notes, dealers said.</p>
<p>HomeSide, based in Jacksonville, Florida, is a full service residential mortgage banking company, formed through the acquisition of the mortgage banking operations of First National Bank of Boston and Barnett Banks Inc.</p>
<p>(( -- Nancy Leinfuss, 212-859-1675 ))</p>
</text>
